-#
  The 'operations.enabled' switch (rollback switch of the maintenance operations: off hides the Fix buttons and refuses
  the applies). Switch::ToggleFormComponent, POST operations/switch, with its state badge (on / off / unknown).
  Locals: return_to ('dashboard': answered with a turbo stream replacing this panel, by its id
  'operations-switch-dashboard'; 'operations': answered with a redirect, the whole /operations page depends on the
  setting). It shows the STORED value (Maintenance.stored_enabled): without the ops DB, or when the value cannot be
  read, it is disabled with the reason shown (never an interactive guess). Always rendered, so that the operations can
  be turned back on.
:ruby
  stored = Maintenance.stored_enabled
  reason = t('maintenance.switch.unreadable') if stored.nil?
  reason = t('maintenance.switch.ops_unavailable') unless Ops.available?
  state = { true => 'on', false => 'off' }.fetch(stored, 'unknown')
  state_css = { 'on' => 'text-bg-success', 'off' => 'text-bg-secondary', 'unknown' => 'text-bg-warning' }
  dashboard = return_to == 'dashboard'
.operations-switch.flex-wrap.align-items-center.gap-2{ id: "operations-switch-#{return_to}",
                                                       class: dashboard ? 'd-flex' : 'd-inline-flex',
                                                       data: { operations_enabled: state == 'unknown' ? 'unknown' : stored.to_s } }
  = render(Switch::ToggleFormComponent.new(url: operations_switch_path, name: 'value', checked: stored == true,
                                           label: t('maintenance.switch.label'), id: "operations-switch-input-#{return_to}",
                                           params: { return_to: }, disabled: reason.present?, reason:, reason_visible: true,
                                           help: t('maintenance.switch.help'),
                                           form_class: ('flex-grow-1' if dashboard), label_class: ('small' if dashboard)))
  %span.badge{ class: state_css[state], data: { operations_state: state } }= t("maintenance.switch.states.#{state}")
